{
  "comment": "OpenCiv2's own assets (docs/NO-INSTALL.md, Music and Sound effects; docs/HD-GRAPHICS.md, Your own heralds): the source of data/native/music, data/native/sound, data/native/heralds, data/native/wonders and data/native/portraits (made by make own-assets, not in the repository), OpenCiv2's repository of assets openciv2/openciv2-assets (repo), its assets/music, assets/sound, assets/heralds, assets/wonders and assets/portraits-historical (MIT, as OpenCiv2: its LICENSE-media, copied as LICENSE; the sound effects' sources CC0: assets/sound/SOURCES.md; the historical portraits' sources public domain or CC0, six AI-generated (MIT): assets/portraits-historical/README.md; the same repository's assets/atlas-hd is the HD art, Peter Johnson's, pinned in data/hd-pack.json) at this commit (sha), each file checked against its SHA-256 and size here. tools/build_own_assets.py fetches them (the files at the commit, from raw.githubusercontent.com) into ~/.cache/openciv2 and copies them as they are, nothing converted; music: CD track number -> the track, Ogg Vorbis as the game plays it (stb_vorbis), copied as data/native/music/trackNN.ogg, which the game plays as CD track NN (with HD graphics first, with Classic graphics where its folder has no Music\\TrackNN: src/platform/sound.c: cd_open_track); heralds: the diplomacy room's animated heralds, copied into data/native/heralds (heralds.txt and the WebPs it names; src/platform/hd.c: hd_herald_find; the local data/native/hd-extra's heralds.txt, where it has the tribe, wins); sound: the sound effects, name.ogg (Ogg Vorbis, 22,050 Hz mono) for the original's Sound\\NAME.WAV, and their credits SOURCES.md, copied into data/native/sound, which the game plays as Sound\\NAME.WAV (with HD graphics first, with Classic graphics where its folder has none: src/platform/sound.c: sound_fallback; files.c: synth_path); wonders: the wonder movies, wonderNN.webp (the picture, an animated WebP) and wonderNN.ogg (the sound, Ogg Vorbis) for the original's Video\\WONDERNN.AVI (NN the wonder's number), copied into data/native/wonders, which the game plays together as that AVI (with HD graphics first, with Classic graphics where its folder has none: src/platform/video.c: open_own_wonder); portraits: the historical leaders' portraits, leader-ID.webp (900x1100) for the original's mk.dll ID (220 + the tribe's slot, a man; 241 + the slot, a woman), and their credits README.md, copied into data/native/portraits, which with HD graphics the diplomacy room, the destroyed civilizations' report and the custom tribe's portrait chooser draw for the tribe's leader (src/platform/hd.c: load_portraits; src/game/hd_graphics.cpp: hd_diplomacy_portrait, hd_portrait_faces); notices: the repository's LICENSE-media, copied as LICENSE beside music, heralds, wonders and portraits (its LICENSE is the HD art's). Upgrading: sha and the files' sha256 and size here (git ls-remote REPO main), then the tool.",
  "repo": "https://github.com/openciv2/openciv2-assets",
  "sha": "c6ed7a0cc00fea08ea174d0848c2d3e508916596",
